---
import LessonLayout from '../../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';
---
<LessonLayout title="Workbook &mdash; Jesus Christ, God and Man" cic="CCC 422-483" scripture="">

<section class="content">

<h2>Student Workbook</h2>
<p class="big-question">For use after class or in a group. Print this page or work in your notebook.</p>

<h3>Remembering the Essentials</h3>

<ol>
<li>What does the name "Jesus" mean in Hebrew? What does that say about his mission?</li>
<li>What is the difference between saying "Jesus is a great teacher" and "Jesus is God made man"? Why does it matter?</li>
<li>What did the Council of Nicaea (325) teach about the nature of Christ?</li>
<li>What does the word "kenosis" mean and how does it apply to Jesus?</li>
<li>Why is it necessary that Jesus be true God and true man for our salvation?</li>
</ol>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>For Reflection and Writing</h3>

<p>Answer each question honestly. There are no "correct" answers to these personal questions.</p>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">1. Who is Jesus to you? Write your personal answer &mdash; not what others say, but what you believe at this moment in your life.</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Do not look for the "perfect" answer. Write from the truth of your heart.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">2. Jesus experienced hunger, fatigue, weeping, anguish, and temptation. How does your prayer change knowing that God understands your pain from within, not just from above?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Think of something you are suffering now. How do you pray differently knowing that Jesus has lived through it?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">3. The kenosis tells us that God emptied himself for love. In what areas of your life do you need to "empty" your ego, your pride, or your need for control?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Be honest. Do not write what you "should" feel, but what you really feel.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">4. Peter confessed that Jesus was the Messiah, but did not understand the cross. Is there something in your faith that you still do not understand or find hard to accept?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Faith is not understanding everything. It is trusting even what is not understood.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">5. If Jesus is truly God and truly man, what does it mean to follow him? Is it optional or the most important decision of your life?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Do not answer what is "expected." Answer what you really live and believe.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content" id="activities">

<h3>Practical Activities</h3>

<h4>A. Lectio Divina with Phil 2:6-11</h4>
<p>Read the hymn of the kenosis slowly, three times. The first time, listen for the word that catches your attention. The second, think how it applies to your life. The third, respond to God with a short prayer. Write the word that most impacted you and why.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>B. The Human Face of God</h4>
<p>Look at a crucifix or an image of Jesus. For 5 minutes, contemplate each detail: the hands, the face, the posture. Then write: "Lord, I see in you..." and complete with what you have discovered.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>C. Letter to Jesus</h4>
<p>Write a letter to Jesus starting with: "Lord, I need you to be God and man because..." Tell him what it means to you that he understands your humanity and has the power to save you.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Memory Verse</h3>

<div class="bible-passage">
<p>"Who, being in very nature God, did not consider equality with God something to be used to his own advantage; rather, he made himself nothing by taking the very nature of a servant, being made in human likeness."</p>
<p class="bible-passage__ref">&mdash; Philippians 2:6-7</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Prayer for This Week</h3>

<blockquote>
<p>Lord Jesus,<br />
you who being God became man,<br />
who emptied your glory for love of us,<br />
help me to know you not only with my mind<br />
but with my heart.<br />
May I see in your cross the greatest love,<br />
and in your resurrection the surest hope.<br />
And that, like Peter, I may confess you<br />
not with learned words,<br />
but with my life laid down.<br />
Amen.</p>
</blockquote>

</section>

